      "name": "OI-dashboards.yml",
      "value": "sections:\n  - title: Inventory\n    description: |\n        This dashboard shows the complete Install Base inventory (Hardware) per customer. It shows all the assets sold to the customers since 2005. The data per customer was extracted using SAVM_SALES_LEVEL_4 associated with it. Inventory includes assets from accounts part of SAVM_SALES_LEVEL_2='Americas_SP'.\n    children:\n      - title: Group Filter\n        description: |\n            Using Group Filters to filter data more accurately and find insights\n        children:\n          - title: Customer Name\n            description: |\n                Filtering based on the customer's name, with the total calculated as the sum of the counts.\n          - title: GU Name\n            description: |\n                Filtering based on the GU name, with the total calculated as the sum of the counts.\n          - title: Contract\n            description: |\n                Filtering based on the Contract Number, with the total calculated as the sum of the counts.\n          - title: Portfolio\n            description: |\n                Filtering based on the Portfolio description, with the total calculated as the sum of the counts.\n          - title: Product Family\n            description: |\n                Filtering based on the Product Family, with the total calculated as the sum of the counts.\n          - title: Equipment Type\n            description: |\n                Filtering based on the Equipment Type, with the total calculated as the sum of the counts.\n          - title: Product Type\n            description: |\n                Filtering based on the Product Type, with the total calculated as the sum of the counts.\n          - title: Coverage\n            description: |\n                Filtering based on Coverage(Covered, Not Covered), with the total calculated as the sum of the counts.\n          - title: Coverage Status\n            description: |\n                Filtering based on Coverage Status, with the total calculated as the sum of the counts.\n          - title: HW Status\n            description: |\n                Filtering based on HW Status, with the total calculated as the sum of the counts.\n          - title: Business Entity\n            description: |\n                Filtering based on which Business Entity it belonged to, with the total calculated as the sum of the counts.\n          - title: Business -Entity\n            description: |\n                Filtering based on which Business -Entity it belonged to, with the total calculated as the sum of the counts.\n      - title: Widgets\n        description: |\n            Using different widgets to display data and insights more accurately.\n        children:\n          - title: Assets by Customer\n            description: |\n                This depicts the full list of assets shipped since 2005 per customer.\n          - title: Assets by Family\n            description: |\n                This depicts the full list of assets shipped since 2005 per product family.\n          - title: Last collected\n            description: |\n                This displays the timestamp of the most recent data collection.\n          - title: Total List Price\n            description: |\n                This displays the total product list price value of all the assets.\n          - title: Product List Price per Product Family\n            description: |\n                A bar chart illustrating the aggregated \"Product List Price\" by Product Family. It displays product families on the horizontal axis and their corresponding total list price for all the devices under the product family on the vertical axis.\n          - title: Product List Price per BE\n            description: |\n                A bar chart illustrating the aggregated \"Product List Price\" by Business Entity. It displays product families on the horizontal axis and their corresponding total list price for all the devices under the Business Entity on the vertical axis.\n          - title: Assets by Coverage Status\n            description: |\n                A multi-bar chart illustrating the distribution of devices by coverage and by covered line status. Possible options:\n\n                    <ol>\n                            <li><b>Covered-Active</b>: Coverage active today.</li>\n                            <li><b>Covered-Overdue</b>: Coverage ended within the last 30 days.</li>\n                            <li><b>Covered-Signed</b>: Coverage starts on a future date. An item will have an active and signed entry if it was renewed before the expiration date.</li>\n                            <li><b>Uncovered-Expired</b>: Coverage ended in the past without an RMA or termination.</li>\n                            <li><b>Uncovered-Terminated</b>: Coverage ended due to an RMA or termination.</li>\n                             <li><b>Uncovered-Not Available</b>: Never covered.</li>\n                    </ol>\n          - title: Assets by HW EOL\n            description: |\n                A pie chart with a distribution of all devices with their current EOL status based on HW Last Day of Support (LDOS). HW status options are \"No EOL\" (No EOL announced), \"Expired\" (Last Day of Support already occurred). Other options represent when the device will be LDOS in the near future.\n          - title: Assets Details\n            description: |\n                A tabular widget which shows detailed asset inventory with quantity, product info, coverage, and hardware status.\n  - title: EOX Notices\n    description: \"Shows all devices that have at least a  HW End of Life announcement.\"\n    children: \n      - title: HW EOL\n        description: \"Shows all devices that have at least a  HW End of Life announcement.\"\n        children: \n          - title: Group Filter\n            description: |\n                Using Group Filters to filter data more accurately and find insights\n            children:\n              - title: Customer Name\n                description: |\n                    Filtering based on the customer's name, with the total calculated as the sum of the counts.\n              - title: GU Name\n                description: |\n                    Filtering based on the GU name, with the total calculated as the sum of the counts.\n              - title: Contract\n                description: |\n                    Filtering based on the Contract Number, with the total calculated as the sum of the counts.\n              - title: Portfolio\n                description: |\n                    Filtering based on the Portfolio description, with the total calculated as the sum of the counts.\n              - title: Product Family\n                description: |\n                    Filtering based on the Product Family, with the total calculated as the sum of the counts.\n              - title: Equipment Type\n                description: |\n                    Filtering based on the Equipment Type, with the total calculated as the sum of the counts.\n              - title: Product Type\n                description: |\n                    Filtering based on the Product Type, with the total calculated as the sum of the counts.\n              - title: Coverage\n                description: |\n                    Filtering based on Coverage(Covered, Not Covered), with the total calculated as the sum of the counts.\n              - title: Coverage Status\n                description: |\n                    Filtering based on Coverage Status, with the total calculated as the sum of the counts.\n              - title: Business Entity\n                description: |\n                    Filtering based on which Business Entity it belonged to, with the total calculated as the sum of the counts.\n              - title: HW Status\n                description: |\n                    Filtering based on HW Status, with the total calculated as the sum of the counts.\n              - title: HW Expiry Year\n                description: |\n                    Filtering based on which year the HW is expiring or expired, with the total calculated as the sum of the counts.\n          - title: Widgets\n            descriptions: |\n                Using different widgets to display data and insights more accurately.\n            children:\n              - title: HW Assets EOL Status\n                description: |\n                    A pie chart with a distribution of all HW Assests on the basis of EOL Status.\n              - title: Last Collected At\n                description: |\n                    This displays the timestamp of the most recent data collection.\n              - title: Total List Price ($)\n                description: |\n                    This displays the total list price value of all the assets.\n              - title: Assets HW EOL Status\n                description: |\n                    This depicts the counter with specific number fof all HW Assests on the basis of EOL Status.\n              - title: HW Status by Equipment Type\n                description: |\n                    A bar graph with a distribution of all HW Assests on the basis of Equipment type and EOL Status.\n              - title: Assets Count by EOLs\n                description: |\n                    This depicts a tabular data with total count using group by on customer_name\",\"product_family\" and \"hw_status to display a combined view.\n              - title: HW Expiry by QTR and Year\n                description: |\n                    This depicts a tabular data with total count of HW Assets expiring in each quearter per year.\n              - title: HW Expiry by Year\n                description: |\n                    This depicts a tabular data with total count of HW Assets expiring per year.\n              - title: Assets HW EOL\n                description: |\n                    This depicts the full list of HW EOls details.\n  - title: Software Licenses\n    description: |\n        This dashboard provides complete information on all software licenses, categorized into two main divisions: Smart and Classic per customer. The data for each customer was extracted using the TOP_LEVEL_DOMAIN associated.\n    children: \n      - title: Group Filter\n        description: |\n            Using Group Filters to filter data more accurately and find insights\n        children:\n          - title: Customer Name\n            description: |\n                Filtering based on the customer's name, with the total calculated as the sum of the counts.\n          - title: Domain\n            description: |\n                Filtering based on domain name, with the total calculated as the sum of the counts.\n          - title: Smart Account\n            description: |\n                Filtering based on Smart Account name, with the total calculated as the sum of the counts.\n          - title: Virtual Account\n            description: |\n                Filtering based on Virtual Account name, with the total calculated as the sum of the counts.\n          - title: Business Entity\n            description: |\n                Filtering based on which Business Entity it belonged to, with the total calculated as the sum of the counts.\n          - title: Business -Entity\n            description: |\n                Filtering based on which Business -Entity it belonged to, with the total calculated as the sum of the counts.\n          - title: PF\n            description: |\n                Filtering based on Product Family, with the total calculated as the sum of the counts.\n          - title: License Status\n            description: |\n                Filtering based on Expiry status, with the total calculated as the sum of the counts.\n          - title: Alerts\n            description: |\n                Filtering based on Alerts status, with the total calculated as the sum of the counts.\n      - title: Widgets\n        descriptions: |\n            Using different widgets to display data and insights more accurately.\n        children:\n          - title: Smart licenses\n            description: |\n                This tab provides all the information related to the smart licenses.\n            children:\n              - title: Smart licenses Status\n                description: |\n                    A pie chart illustrating all the smart license with their current Expiration status. Expiration status options are \"Valid indefinitely\" (No EOL announced), \"Expired\" (Last Day of Support already occurred). Other options represent when device will be LDOS in the near future.\n              - title: Business Entity\n                description: |\n                    A pie chart that depicts the breakdown of SMART licenses accross the different Business Entities.\n              - title: Smart License Last collected Data\n                description: |\n                    This displays the timestamp of the most recent data collection.\n              - title: Smart License Summary\n                description: |\n                    A tabular widget which displays the different license groups with their respective totals, usage, availability, EOL status, and alerts.\n                children:  \n                  - title: Total Smart Licenses\n                    description: |\n                        This depicts the total number of smart licenses.\n                  - title: Consumed Smart License\n                    description: |\n                        This depicts the total number of smart licenses that are currently in use.\n                  - title: Available Smart License\n                    description: |\n                        This depicts the total number of smart licenses that are currently available.\n                  - title: Smart License Device Details\n                    description: |\n                        A detailed overview of smart license device information, including account, license, product, and scription details along with status and key dates.\n          - title: Classic licenses\n            description: |\n                This tab provides all the information related to the Classic licenses.\n            children:\n              - title: Classic licenses Status\n                description: |\n                    A pie chart illustrating all the classic license groups with their current Expiration status. Expiration status options are \"Valid indefinitely\" (No EOL announced), \"Expired\" (Last Day of Support already occurred). Other options represent when device will be LDOS in the near future.\n              - title: Business Entity\n                description: |\n                    A pie chart that depicts the breakdown of Classic licenses accross the different Business Entities.\n              - title: Classic License Last collected Data\n                description: |\n                    This displays the timestamp of the most recent data collection.\n              - title: Classic License Summary\n                description: |\n                    A tabular widget which displays the different license groups with their respective totals, usage, availability, EOL status, and alerts.\n                children:  \n                  - title: Total Classic Licenses\n                    description: |\n                        This depicts the total number of classic licenses.\n                  - title: Consumed Classic License\n                    description: |\n                        This depicts the total number of classic licenses that are currently in use.\n                  - title: Available Classic License\n                    description: |\n                        This depicts the total number of classic licenses that are currently available.\n                  - title: Classic License Device Details\n                    description: |\n                        A detailed overview of classic license device information, including account, license, product, and scription details along with status and key dates.\n  - title: Security Advisories\n    description: |\n        The Security Advisories dashboard provides an overview of all security advisories, showing their status, severity, and impact to help manage device vulnerabilities.\n    children:\n      - title: Group Filter\n        description: |\n            Using Group Filters to filter data more accurately and find insights\n        children:\n          - title: Customer Name\n            description: |\n                Filtering based on the customer's name, with the total calculated as the sum of the counts.\n          - title: Contract\n            description: |\n                Filtering based on the Contract Number, with the total calculated as the sum of the counts.\n          - title: Product Name\n            description: |\n                Filtering based on the Product Name, with the total calculated as the sum of the counts.\n          - title: Product Family\n            description: |\n                Filtering based on the Product Family, with the total calculated as the sum of the counts.\n          - title: PSirt ID\n            description: |\n                Filtering based on the PSirt IDs, with the total calculated as the sum of the counts.\n          - title: SW Version\n            description: |\n                Filtering based on the SW Version, with the total calculated as the sum of the counts.\n          - title: SW OS Type\n            description: |\n                Filtering based on the SW OS Type, with the total calculated as the sum of the counts.\n          - title: Security Advisory Status\n            description: |\n                Filtering based on the Security Advisory Status, with the total calculated as the sum of the counts.\n          - title: Security Advisory Severity\n            description: |\n                Filtering based on the Security Advisory Severity, with the total calculated as the sum of the counts.\n      - title: Widgets\n        description: |\n            Using different widgets to display data and insights more accurately.\n        children:\n          - title: Total Assets Impacted\n            description: |\n                This depicts the total number of devices within the network that are affected by security advisories or vulnerabilities.\n          - title: Security Advisory Severity\n            description: |\n                The pie chart visually represents the distribution of security advisories by severity levels such as Not Available, Medium, High, and Critical\n          - title: Security Advisory Status\n            description: |\n                This depicts the distribution of security advisories based on Potentially Vulnerable, Vulnerable status.\n          - title: Total Sec Adv Bulletins\n            description: |\n                This provides a cumulative count of all security advisory bulletins issued\n          - title: Security Advisory Status by Severity\n            description: |\n                The bar graph depicts the distribution of security advisories categorized by their severity levels, such as Not Available, Medium, High, and Critical\n          - title: Devices Count by Security Advisories\n            description: |\n                The \"Devices Count by Security Advisories\" table depicts the number of devices impacted by each security advisory ID along with their Status and Severity. This has a drill down dashboard for more information on impacted devices.\n            children:\n              - title: Security Advisories Drill Down\n                description: |\n                    This dashboard depicts the details of a PSirt ID and total number of devices within the network that are affected by it.\n                children:\n                  - title: Group Filter\n                    description: |\n                        Using Group Filters to filter data more accurately and find insights\n                    children:\n                      - title: Equipment Type\n                        description: |\n                            Filtering based on the Equipment Type, with the total calculated as the sum of the counts.\n                      - title: Product ID\n                        description: |\n                            Filtering based on the Product ID, with the total calculated as the sum of the counts.\n                      - title: SW OS Type\n                        description: |\n                            Filtering based on the SW OS Type, with the total calculated as the sum of the counts.\n                      - title: SW Version\n                        description: |\n                            The \"Assets with Security Advisories\" table depicts the list of assets affected by security advisories with status Vulnerable, Potentially Vulnerable and Severity as High. It also displays Contract Number, SW OS Type, SW Version and Customer Name.\n                      - title: Security Advisory Status\n                        description: |\n                            Filtering based on the Security Advisory Status, with the total calculated as the sum of the counts.\n                      - title: Security Advisory Severity\n                        description: |\n                            Filtering based on the Security Advisory Severity, with the total calculated as the sum of the counts.\n                  - title: Widgets\n                    description: |\n                        Using different widgets to display data and insights more accurately.\n                    children:\n                      - title: PSirtID\n                        description: |\n                            It represents the PsirtId that is the focus of the drill-down view displayed in this dashboard.\n                      - title: Total Device Count\n                        description: |\n                            Total number of devices affected by the specifc PsirtID\n                      - title: Security Advisories Details\n                        description: |\n                            The table displays detailed information about the specifc PsirtID with the devices associated with it. \n          - title: Assets with Security Advisories\n            description: |\n               This table depicts the list of devices with reference to a security advisory with the highest Security Advisory Status(if present). It shows the association between Product name and PsirtID categorized by their severity, status,SW version, OS Type etc.\n  - title: SW EOL\n    description: |\n        This dashboard provides complete information of all the devices that have an actual SW EOL including their contract number, SW version etc, along with there EOL records. \n    children: \n      - title: Group Filter\n        description: |\n            Using Group Filters to filter data more accurately and find insights\n        children:\n          - title: Customer Name\n            description: |\n                Filtering based on the customer's name, with the total calculated as the sum of the counts.\n          - title: Contract\n            description: |\n                Filtering based on the Contract Number, with the total calculated as the sum of the counts.\n          - title: Equipment Type\n            description: |\n                Filtering based on the Equipment Type, with the total calculated as the sum of the counts.\n          - title: Product Name\n            description: |\n                Filtering based on the Product Name, with the total calculated as the sum of the counts.\n          - title: Product Family\n            description: |\n                Filtering based on the Product Family, with the total calculated as the sum of the counts.\n          - title: SW Version\n            description: |\n                Filtering based on the SW Version, with the total calculated as the sum of the counts.\n          - title: SW OS Type\n            description: |\n                Filtering based on the SW OS Type, with the total calculated as the sum of the counts.\n          - title: SW Bulletin Number\n            description: |\n                Filtering based on the Bulletin Number, with the total calculated as the sum of the counts.\n          - title: SW EOL Status\n            description: |\n                Filtering based on the EOL Status, with the total calculated as the sum of the counts.\n          - title: SW Expiry Year\n            description: |\n                Filtering based on the SW Expiry Year, with the total calculated as the sum of the counts.      \n      - title: Widgets\n        descriptions: |\n            Using different widgets to display data and insights more accurately.\n        children:\n          - title: Summary\n            description: |\n                This tab provides all the information related to the assets along with their EOL details.\n            children:\n              - title: Assets EOL Status\n                description: |\n                    A pie chart illustrating all the assets with their EOL status. Expiration status options are \"Expired\", \"Expiring in a Quater\", \"Expiring in 4 Quaters\", \"Expiring in 8 Quaters\" and \"Expiring after 8 Quaters\".\n              - title: Assets SW EOL Status\n                description: |\n                    A counter widget that depicts the expiration status of all the assets.\n              - title: Last collected Data\n                description: |\n                    This displays the timestamp of the most recent data collection.\n              - title: SW Status by Product Family\n                description: |  \n                    This depicts a bar chart with a distribution of all the assets on the basis of Product Family and EOL Status.\n              - title: Assets Count by EOLs\n                description: |\n                    This depicts a tabular data with total count using group by on customer_name\",\"product_name\" and \"sw_status to display a combined view.\n              - title: SW Expiry by QTR and Year\n                description: |\n                    A bar chart which depicts the SW Assets expiring in each quarter per year starting from 2025.\n              - title: SW Expiry by Year\n                description: |\n                    A bar chart which depicts the SW Assets expiring per year starting from 2025.           \n              - title: Assets SW EOLs\n                description: |\n                    A tabular widget which displays all the information related to a product including the name, product family, sw version, os type, bulletin number, EOL details etc.\n          - title: Details\n            description: |\n                This tab provides all the information related to the EOL of products.\n            children:\n              - title: SW EOLs\n                description: |\n                    A tabular widget which displays all the information related to a product including the name, product family, sw version, os type, bulletin number, EOL details etc.\n  - title: Instructions for uploading data to Software EOL and Security Advisory\n    description:  |\n        1. Navigate to the Inventory dashboard. <br>\n        2. In the top-right corner, click the control box icon next to the three dots.  <br><img src=\"/iconlib/control_box\" width=\"900\"><br>\n        3. Select the 'Unique PID Groups' checkbox and click 'Apply'.  <br><img src=\"/iconlib/control_table\" width=\"900\"><br>\n        4. A new table will appear at the bottom of the dashboard.  <br>\n        5. Apply filters at the top of the dashboard based on customer, COVERED status, contract, or portfolio as needed.  <br>\n        6. In the top-right corner of this table widget, click the three dots icon and select 'Export' to download the table.  <br>\n        7. In the downloaded file, populate the 'OS type' and 'OS version' columns for the devices you need to evaluate.  <br>\n        8. Do not alter any other column names. <br>\n        9. Navigate to the Software Data dashboard.  <br>\n        10. In the top-right corner of the widget, click the 'Add' button. <br>\n        11. Browse for and upload the prepared CSV file.  <br>\n        12. The system will begin processing the data via a pipeline, and the uploaded information will become visible in the dashboards shortly thereafter.  <br>\n"
